LOK: Impress tables report every edge's bounds; the left edge drags

A LOK client draws its own table borders from
LOK_CALLBACK_TABLE_SELECTED and clamps a drag to the bounds it reads.
Impress sent bounds only for inner edges, and its row minimum was the
layouter's fixed 600 (a todo), not the row's own minimum height; a
client's guide and the kernel's result then disagreed. The JSON now
carries leftMin/leftMax and rightMin/rightMax for both axes (columns
only left to right) and inner rows use the row's minimum height.
The leftmost column edge did nothing (DragEdge's own todo) while
adding an undo step. Over LOK's TableChangeCurrentBorderPosition it now
narrows or widens the first column and moves the table with its edge,
as the top edge also moves it, in the same undo step. Desktop drag
handles are unchanged.

diff --git a/svx/source/table/svdotable.cxx b/svx/source/table/svdotable.cxx
--- a/svx/source/table/svdotable.cxx
+++ b/svx/source/table/svdotable.cxx
@@ -1579,8 +1579,30 @@
 
 void SdrTableObj::changeEdge(bool bHorizontal, int nEdge, sal_Int32 nOffset)
 {
-    if (mpImpl.is())
+    if (!mpImpl.is() || !mpImpl->mxTable.is())
+        return;
+    const bool bLeft = !bHorizontal && nEdge == 0 && GetWritingMode() != WritingMode_RL_TB;
+    if (!bLeft)
         mpImpl->DragEdge(bHorizontal, nEdge, nOffset);
+    else
+    {
+        // LOK: the left edge narrows the first column.
+        try
+        {
+            const sal_Int32 nWidth = mpImpl->mpLayouter->getColumnWidth(0) - nOffset;
+            Reference<XIndexAccess> xCols(mpImpl->mxTable->getColumns(), UNO_QUERY_THROW);
+            Reference<XPropertySet> xCol(xCols->getByIndex(0), UNO_QUERY_THROW);
+            xCol->setPropertyValue(u"Size"_ustr, Any(nWidth));
+        }
+        catch (const Exception&)
+        {
+            TOOLS_WARN_EXCEPTION("svx.table", "");
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+    // A first edge moves the table with it.
+    if (nEdge == 0 && (bHorizontal || bLeft))
+        NbcMove(bHorizontal ? Size(0, nOffset) : Size(nOffset, 0));
 }
 
